msgid "Main cable for SF10 Rangefinder"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:38
#: 79c53a1b5fb74686b7b644c7f64b1e6e
msgid "Serial connection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:40
#: 97408e1d2d6343b9a391258e02ca4b62
msgid "For a serial connection you can use any spare UART. Connect the RX line of the UART to the TX line of the Lidar, and the TX line of the UART to the RX line of the Lidar. Also connect the GND and 5V lines. You do not need flow control pins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:45
#: 80a0ed2f55aa4d74b3a109ada13bb48d
msgid "The diagram below shows how to connect to SERIAL4."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:50
#: bc2875a2a2254f0da7173b0711b633be
msgid "Pixhawk and SF10Rangefinder: Serial Connection (SERIAL4)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:52
#: 2ba997c474b4473ba1411900b945951a
msgid "You then need to setup the serial port and rangefinder parameters. If you have used the SERIAL4/5 port on the Pixhawk then you would set the following parameters in the case of the first rangefinder(this is done in the *Mission Planner* **Config/Tuning \\| Full Parameter List** page):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:57
#: bd388134ec534c5e9e850b8262e84027
msgid ":ref:`SERIAL4_PROTOCOL <SERIAL4_PROTOCOL>` = 9 (Lidar)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:58
#: e0112d529cba41aa88f3097c91bf2b2e
msgid ":ref:`SERIAL4_BAUD <SERIAL4_BAUD>` = 115 (115200 baud)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:59
#: 742af548280645da8767dce201228bcd
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_TYPE <RNGFND1_TYPE>` = 8 (LightWareSerial)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:60
#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:87
#: ecbd8275665f4d92827d327191a7f10c
#: 26139fd759c342ac8ba2261d789a776c
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_SCALING <RNGFND1_SCALING>` = 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:61
#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:88
#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:126
#: 7192f165d4ef4b21ad6690b2fc7c2dd6
#: b5278f0347e543f98f43b9cddea4b269
#: 12f46ad2ad24437981aa4bdaf61ae077
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_MIN <RNGFND1_MIN>` = 0.05"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:62
#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:89
#: 43d4e0031afc4f16b7324ae09fa5cb5b
#: 14afef160d4d4e16b733c56e3e3b690e
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_MAX <RNGFND1_MAX>` = **25** (for SF10A), **50** (for SF10B), **100** (for SF10C) or **120** (for SF11C).  *This is the distance in meters that the rangefinder can reliably read. The value depends on the model of the lidar.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:63
#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:90
#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:128
#: 43e34e67d6fd4ef88e5522b9f704e4cf
#: 7f43a0bdef2d41abb874d07caec10ac8
#: 426f3547bed94769a60e230728d1812a
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_GNDCLR <RNGFND1_GNDCLR>` = 0.1 *or more accurately the distance in metres from the range finder to the ground when the vehicle is landed.  This value depends on how you have mounted the rangefinder.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:65
#: a1a2838c077c40bc83357704060ff6ea
msgid "If you instead were using the Telem2 port on the Pixhawk then you would set :ref:`SERIAL2_PROTOCOL <SERIAL2_PROTOCOL>` = 9, and :ref:`SERIAL2_BAUD <SERIAL2_BAUD>` = 115"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:67
#: 846485295d6343899097710742bcc79b
msgid "Lightware lidars manufactured before May 2018 shipped with a default baud rate of 19200. If your device was produced before this date, you will need to set the baud rate to 19200 (Parameter value 19). Alternatively, you may reconfigure your lightware device to use a baudrate of 115200 using the Lightware Terminal application and use the settings above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:72
#: 1031f50f9b0d4a74a88590a8579012a9
msgid "I2C connection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:74
#: 3801b6e612034000aa3c26bf4bed5b67
msgid "Connect the SDA line of the Lidar to the SDA line of the I2C port on the Pixhawk, and the SCL line of the Lidar to the SCL line of the I2C port. Also connect the GND and 5V lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:79
#: 6673a40caaeb4365af906f45aeaae616
msgid "Pixhawk and SF10 Rangefinder: I2CConnection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:81
#: 8cec5efa6db54ac8841726353c5230fc
msgid "You then need to configure the rangefinder parameters as shown below (this is done in the *Mission Planner* **Config/Tuning \\| Full Parameter List** page):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:85
#: 1712f6bd62c14e79ac7984d5fa3432b6
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_TYPE <RNGFND1_TYPE>` = 7 (LightWareI2C)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:86
#: 2dcea101716e44cea8fd6105dbaaebb2
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_ADDR <RNGFND1_ADDR>` = 102 (I2C Address of lidar in decimal).  *Please note that this setting is in decimal and not hexadecimal as shown in the lidar settings screen. The default address is 0x66 which is 102 in decimal.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:92
#: b267f3eb5c84457199fd6436e019796d
msgid "It may be necessary to enable the sensor's \"I2C compatibility mode (Pixhawk)\".  This can be done by connecting the lidar to your PC using a USB cable, then download `Lightware Studio <https://lightwarelidar.com/pages/lightware-studio>`__, connect and check the checkbox shown below"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:100
#: a8bb800a1a5d40778ea53f49ebc87b33
msgid "The default I2C address was 85 (0x55 in hexadecimal) on older LightWare rangefinders. This was changed to prevent conflict with another device on ArduPilot. Please check your rangefinder system settings to determine what your I2C address is."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:107
#: 113fa02bd5644b46a72c4daeb0faf5ea
msgid "Analog connection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:109
#: c81ea5a490634642a7a11f1d9d290639
msgid "The SF10's Analog Out pin (5) should be connected to the Pixhawk's 3.3V ADC (analog to digital converter).  The Pixhawk will provide the regulated 5V power supply needed by the sensor using the 5V and GND pins of the ADC connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:117
#: 3d4795ea994a4dd8802f611db6be8f9a
msgid "Pixhawk and SF10 Rangefinder:Analog Connection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:119
#: 64ccc812ddd249c0ac49395a15883de7
msgid "You then need to setup the ADC and rangefinder parameters as shown below (this is done in the *Mission Planner* **Config/Tuning \\| Full Parameter List** page):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:123
#: 29f36b1d143b4516bcad9c939c3344f2
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_TYPE <RNGFND1_TYPE>` = 1 (Analog)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:124
#: b0d9e430ccf84011ba472efaa0eeadd0
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_PIN <RNGFND1_PIN>` = 14 (2nd pin of 3.3V ADC connector)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:125
#: df90799e7e714bf3b473df822282d66d
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_SCALING <RNGFND1_SCALING>` = **9.76** (for SF10A), **19.531** (for SF10B), **39.06** (for SF10C), **46.87** (for SF11C)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:127
#: 2e88c700d9ce409ba9d3db4b31c6e55e
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_MAX <RNGFND1_MAX>` = **20** (for SF10A), **45** (for SF10B), **95** (for SF10C) or **115** (for SF11C).  *This is the distance in meters that the rangefinder can reliably read. The value depends on the model of the lidar.  Note the range is 5m less than using Serial or I2C protocols so that out-of-range can be reliably detected*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:130
#: b65a27964b2449b4b84a7b7cec5e7e51
msgid "The :ref:`RNGFND1_SCALING <RNGFND1_SCALING>` value depends on the voltage on the rangefinders output pin at the maximum range. By default the SF10/B will output 2.56V at 50m, so the scaling factor is 50m / 2.56v ≈ 19.53 (the analog distance range for each of the rangefinder variants can be found in the `SF10 Manual <http://documents.lightware.co.za/SF10%20-%20Laser%20Altimeter%20Manual%20-%20Rev%2011.pdf>`__). The manual explains how you can confirm and change the maximum output range/voltage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lightware-sf10-lidar.rst:136
#: 7344dba8e3a148aaa70c33c3ced3d4b0
msgid "We highly recommend that you tune the ``RNGFND1_SCALING`` value by comparing the output against a known distance."
msgstr ""

